  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n \nThe upper high will continue to shift to the south and west Monday. \nThe airmass over South-Central Texas will remain about the same with \nlow level flow from the east to southeast. Temperatures will be \nstagnant through the beginning of next week. It will continue to \nfeel like an endless summer rather than the start of fall. Models \nare still showing the first real Pacific cold front of the season \nmoving into TX, but the timing is not consistent. Now it's looking \nlater in the week. Despite this change there are still chances for \nwidespread rain starting Tuesday and extending into Friday. They are \nalso showing signs of possible heavy area at times during this \nperiod. Northerly to northeasterly winds will bring cooler, drier \nair. High temperatures for the second half of the week may be below \n90 for most of the CWA, but low temperatures have trended a little \nwarmer and mostly above 70.",
